High-resolution (600 dpi) image of strangewayes' print-ready errata card for [[Blast The Door, Kid! (PC Errata 3)]] (the card with its Players Committee errata text and the errata mark) (A New Hope, Light Side), from [[Strangewayes|strangewayes]]' [[Fan projects#HiRez scanning project|HiRez scanning project]].

Source: strangewayes' HiRez scanning project — forum thread [https://swccg.com/snapshots/forum/t65510.html HiRez scanning duty (t65510)]; original TIFF [https://drive.usercontent.google.com/uc?id=1CaIXJ9UsrpD1RrfvDuxutyZAKJJEnL05&export=download Blast The Door Kid _ E.tif].

Original TIFF: <code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere;white-space:normal">Blast The Door Kid _ E.tif</code>, 1497×2073 px at 600 dpi, 9,340,940 bytes, SHA-256 <code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere;white-space:normal">d9183e203f0305d2ed27ecb2a0955da085c89f4e307e4f7c4d425f7e76fd73cb</code>.

Changes from the TIFF: converted to WebP (quality 90); the card's rounded corners masked to transparent (anti-aliased; corner radii measured from the image, 44.0, 47.5, 72.5, 57.0 px); resized: no; no other change.

The regular face of this card on its article stays [[:File:ANH-L-blastthedoorkid.gif]]; this fan rendition is retained as a qualified comparison.

Credit: image by strangewayes for the HiRez scanning project; used here with credit to that project. Fair use rationale: this is an image of a copyrighted Star Wars Customizable Card Game card, © Lucasfilm Ltd. and Decipher Inc. (card design by the Players Committee). It is used only to identify and study the card on this non-commercial fan wiki, it does not replace any product sold today, and no free equivalent exists.

[[Category:High-res card scans]]

Native comparison shows re-typeset text and a gold E within the card. Official gallery marks and external white E/D-E1 marks differ. This is a credited fan print-ready rendition, not a scan of any official source image; its rendition differences do not create another official PC image ordinal.
The native TIFF prints the later remainder/simultaneous wording with a comma after “for remainder of battle”, as on the 2017 partial; the full E and D-E1 faces omit that comma. This fan punctuation and its gold in-card E do not establish an official image identity.